<title>USA: BioSafe gets $800,000 arbitration award.</title>
<headline>BioSafe gets $800,000 arbitration award.</headline>
<dateline>CAMBRIDGE, Mass 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>BioSafe International Inc said Wednesday it had received an award worth about $800,000 in the arbitration of its claims against Richard Rosen, the company's former chairman, chief executive officer and president.</p>
<p>BioSafe, a solid waste management company, said the arbitrator found that Rosen had failed to discharge in good faith the duties of his executive positions and also failed to act under the direction of the company's board of directors.</p>
<p>At the request of the company's board, Rosen resigned from BioSafe on March 27, 1996, it said.</p>
